SUMMARY:Community Writing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive space! \nA Writers Collective of Canada (WCC) workshop is unlike any other. We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, listen deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into your story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, and respect.wcc-cec.org \nNo experience required. Materials are provided. Beginners are welcome! Register via https://tpl.ca/locations/DA/ or by calling the Danforth/Coxwell branch at 416-393-7783.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/community-writing-workshop/
LOCATION:Danforth/Coxwell Library\, 1675 Danforth Avenue\, Toronto\, M4C 4Y4
ORGANIZER;CN="Danforth Coxwell Branch%2C Toronto Public Library":MAILTO:dastaff@tpl.ca
END:VEVENT
